      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "For me on Linux/Proton (build 1722) in Desktop Mode with a Switch Pro Controller over USB (both with and without Steam Input) the Controls menu shows an Xbox controller as expected.\n\nMaybe of note, is that the Controls menu does not refresh to the new input type until re-opened from the sidebar. Even closing and re-opening the Main Menu or changing tabs does not cause it to refresh; only the sidebar will.\n\nStill doesn't explain why it would show the SteamVR page in the first place, though. Just a thought, could the built-in Gamepad Support add-on in SteamVR have something to do with it, even without SteamVR running?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
